            <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold mt-8 mb-3">What Is a Salary Slip?</h2>
            <p>
                A <strong>salary slip</strong> (also called pay slip or payslip) is
                a document your employer gives you every month showing:
            </p>
            <ul class="list-disc pl-6 space-y-2">
                <li>Basic salary</li>
                <li>Allowances (house rent, medical, transport)</li>
                <li>Deductions (income tax, EOBI, provident fund)</li>
                <li>Net pay (what actually lands in your bank account)</li>
            </ul>
            <p>
                When you use our{" "}
                <a
                    href="/tools/salary-tax-calculator/"
                    class="text-blue-600 hover:underline font-medium"
                >
                    Salary Tax Calculator
                </a>
                , you can cross-check the "income tax" line on your salary slip to
                make sure your employer is deducting the correct amount.
            </p>

